<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Russo-Turkish War (1828–1829)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1828">1828</a>–<a href="/years/1829">1829</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Russo-Turkish War of 1828–1829 was fought between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russian-empire">Russian Empire</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire</a>, provoked partly by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greek-war-of-independence">Greek War of Independence</a>. Russian armies crossed the Balkan mountains and took Adrianople in August 1829, while in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caucasus">Caucasus</a> they took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kars">Kars</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/erzurum">Erzurum</a>. The Treaty of Adrianople gave <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/danube">Danube</a> delta and forced the Ottomans to accept Greek autonomy.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/russo-turkish-war-1828-1829.jpg" alt="Russo-Turkish War (1828–1829)" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: January Suchodolski · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:January_Suchodolski_-_Akhaltsikhe_siege.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
